==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|berô|bear|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|bʰer-|brown animal|lang=ang}}. Cognate with Old High German ''[[bero]]'' (German ''[[Bär]]''), Middle Dutch ''[[bere]]'' (Dutch ''[[beer#Dutch|beer]]''), Old Norse ''[[ber]]''. A North Germanic variant, ''*bernu-'', gave Old Norse {{Latinx|[[bjǫrn]]}} (Swedish ''[[björn]]'').

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈberɑ/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=m}}

# [[bear]]

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-n-m|ber}}

====Descendants====
